  "about": "Differences from the frozen baseline (variant_output_baseline, see baseline_manifest.json) that are known, explained and accepted. OQ-ARCH-15: the baseline does not move for the rest of the port, so departures are enumerated and justified here rather than absorbed by re-baselining. A part NOT listed here is a failure by default -- silence is not acceptance. This file says each difference is CORRECT, not that it is small; whether the accumulated total is acceptable is the reviewed sign-off at the PartDesign end state, which OQ-ARCH-15 places later.",
  "established": "2026-08-18",
  "established_from": "full 576-part render at commit fcfeefa, 3 h 7 min, compared against baseline_manifest.json; 221 of 576 parts differed, 0 missing, 0 added, 0 unreadable",
  "accepted": [
    {
      "id": "oq-des-b13-panel-tolerance-off-the-mating-face",
      "commit": "299633c",
      "date": "2026-08-14",
      "design_ref": "OQ-DES-B13; see also OQ-DES-C5",
      "why": "panel_tolerance is a real clearance, but for the panel: it is the panel/corner and panel/bulkhead gap, so the panel's outer surface still lands flush with the mold line at corner_radius. What it is NOT is the corner/bulkhead clearance -- that interface is OQ-DES-C5 and carries corner_tolerance, held at 0. The defect was panel_tolerance appearing on a third interface it does not govern. The corner's rectangular panel extension stopped one panel_tolerance short of flat_x, so in the band where the corner radius has already curved inside flat_x the corner was cut off and the bulkhead stood over it; the bulkhead's matching cleanup carried an eps that cut a material face 0.01 mm too deep. Both are halves of one fix and the commit says so. The two parts are cut by the same polygon, which is why the same 0.1 mm appears in both.",
      "measured": "surface distance 0.100000 mm on the bulkhead and 0.100010 mm on the corner; bounding box moves by exactly 0.1000 mm on the 24 corners where the change reaches an extreme, and not at all on the rest, where it is internal. 0.1 mm is panel_tolerance, which is unscaled, so the figure is the same at every U. Relative volume 1.1e-6 to 1.7e-3.",
      "verified": "the corner was bisected commit by commit against extracted libraries: 9bc386b reproduces the baseline exactly at 1202.6214 mm^3 / 17,324 triangles / bbox -6.15, and 299633c gives 1202.8714 / 17,316 / -6.25",
